IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Life Insurance Act 1995 (Cth) -- what a person insured, or owning a policy, meets in the Act: what counts as a life policy
-- and so what a life insurer may offer (ss 9, 9A, 234), who owns the policy (s 10) and what a policy inside super is
-- (Dictionary, "superannuation policy"), who may take out a policy young (s 199), children's advancement policies (ss 218-220),
-- what an assignment needs (s 200), protection from creditors (ss 204, 205), surrender, paid-up and non-forfeiture rights
-- (ss 207, 209, 210), payment on death without probate (ss 211-213), no set-off of other policies (s 217), lost policy
-- documents (s 221), suicide and war-service terms (ss 228, 229).
--
-- SEAT: the insured person, or the owner of the policy -- for Chloe, the fund member whose life is insured under her fund's
-- group cover. Every decision is phrased as that person would ask it: "Is my cover a life policy?", "Do I own my policy?",
-- "May my insurer forfeit my policy?", "May my insurer pay my family without probate?". Where the Act addresses only the
-- insurer, ASIC, APRA or a court (ss 207(3), 210(5), 211, 213, 221(5)), the decision says what that means for the person.
-- Where the Act hands a judgment to someone else (the company "satisfied" of entitlement, s 211(1)(d), (e); APRA's
-- suspension, s 208), the answer is conditional on it, asked as a fact.
--
-- Provisions covered: s 9(1)(a), (e), (2); s 9A(1)-(7); s 10(2); s 199(1), (2); s 200(2); s 204(1)-(3); s 205(1), (3);
-- s 207(1)-(4), (6); s 208 (as a fact); s 209(1)-(3); s 210(1), (2), (5); s 211(1), (5); s 212(1), (5); s 213(1)-(4), (6), (7);
-- s 217; s 218(1); s 219(2)-(4); s 220(1), (2); s 221(5); s 228; s 229; s 234; Dictionary, "superannuation policy" (a), "child".
--
-- Edition: Life Insurance Act 1995, Compilation No. 69, compilation date 21 February 2025 (register id C2025C00135), as
-- deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A04860.txt. No regulations are deposited: the amounts the regulations may
-- prescribe instead of the Act's $100,000 (ss 211, 212) and $50,000 (s 213), and the prudential-standards surrender floor
-- (s 207(4)), are INPUTS here, with the Act's figures used in the cases.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: registration, statutory funds, financial management, monitoring, judicial and statutory management, winding up,
-- transfers and amalgamations, prudential standards and directions (Parts 2A-9, 10A, 11 except s 234, 12) -- machinery or
-- prudential, addressed to the company; s 198 (ASIC and policy forms); ss 201-203 (mortgages, trusts, change of trustee);
-- Division 2A (structured settlements); s 9(1)(b)-(d), (f), (g) (annuities, investment contracts); ss 12A, 12B except as a fact;
-- s 210(3), (4), (6)-(9) (interest on overdue premiums, increases in sum insured); ss 214-216A (the company's discharge, payment
-- into Court, unclaimed money); ss 222-227 (replacement document form, registers); s 230 (stated in NOTES.md, not asserted).
-- Who may be insured -- insurable interest in one's own life, a spouse's, a child's -- is NOT in this Act; it is the Insurance
-- Contracts Act 1984 Part III. Nominating beneficiaries is NOT in this Act either: inside super it is the SIS Act s 59(1A) and
-- reg 6.17A (encoded in that Act's baseline); outside super it is the policy's terms. Whether a fund may give a member cover at
-- all (the under-25, low-balance and inactive-account bars, the MySuper default) is the SIS Act ss 68AA-68AAD, not this Act.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the individual
-- to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test
-- pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Life Insurance Act 1995 -- the insured person and the policy owner`

-- `the later of` (two dates) and DATE PLUS a number of days come from the daydate library.

§§ `9, 9A, 234 -- is my cover a life policy, and may a life insurer offer it to me`

-- s 9(1): "each of the following constitutes a life policy ... (a) a contract of insurance that provides for the payment of money
-- on the death of a person or on the happening of a contingency dependent on the termination or continuance of human life; ...
-- (e) a continuous disability policy". (2): a death contract is not a life policy if "(a) ... the duration of the contract is
-- to be not more than one year; and (b) payment is only to be made in the event of: (i) death by accident; or (ii) death
-- resulting from a specified sickness."
-- s 9A(1): a continuous disability policy is a contract of insurance "(a) that is, by its terms, to be of more than 3 years'
-- duration; and (b) under which a benefit is payable in the event of: (i) the death, by accident or by some other cause stated
-- in the contract, of the person whose life is insured ...; or (ii) injury to, or disability of, the insured as a result of
-- accident or sickness; or (iii) the insured being found to have a stated condition or disease." (2): a shorter contract
-- qualifies if contracts of its kind "are usually of more than 3 years' duration" and it is shorter "only because of the age of
-- the owner". (3): not if the terms "permit alteration, at the instance of the life company ... of the benefits ... or the
-- premiums"; (4), (5): except alterations that only improve benefits on an offer the owner accepts, or premium alterations made
-- "on a simultaneous and consistent basis" across all contracts of the kind. (6): not consumer credit insurance; (7): not
-- health insurance.
-- Gloss: income protection, trauma and disability cover is a "life policy" only if it is a continuous disability policy --
-- guaranteed for more than 3 years, the insurer unable to reprice one person alone.
DECLARE `My cover` HAS
    `it pays money on a death` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it pays on a death only if by accident or a specified sickness` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it pays on my injury or disability, or on my being found to have a stated condition` IS A BOOLEAN
    `its term in years` IS A NUMBER
    `cover of its kind usually runs over 3 years and it is shorter only because of my age at entry` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the insurer may alter its benefits or premiums` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the only alterations allowed are improvements I accept, or premium changes made simultaneously and consistently for all such contracts` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is consumer credit insurance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is health insurance` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `A kind of policy` IS ONE OF
    `a life policy because it pays on a death (s 9(1)(a))`
    `a life policy because it is a continuous disability policy (s 9(1)(e), s 9A)`
    `not a life policy under this Act`

GIVEN `the cover` IS A `My cover`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a continuous disability policy` IF
        (    `the cover`'s `its term in years` GREATER THAN 3
         OR  `the cover`'s `cover of its kind usually runs over 3 years and it is shorter only because of my age at entry`)
    AND (    `the cover`'s `it pays money on a death`
         OR  `the cover`'s `it pays on my injury or disability, or on my being found to have a stated condition`)
    AND (    (NOT `the cover`'s `the insurer may alter its benefits or premiums`)
         OR  `the cover`'s `the only alterations allowed are improvements I accept, or premium changes made simultaneously and consistently for all such contracts`)
    AND (NOT `the cover`'s `it is consumer credit insurance`)
    AND (NOT `the cover`'s `it is health insurance`)

@export Is my cover a life policy under the Life Insurance Act 1995 (ss 9, 9A)?
GIVEN `the cover` IS A `My cover` @desc What your cover pays on, how long it runs, and whether the insurer can change it
GIVETH A `A kind of policy`
DECIDE `What kind of policy is my cover` IS
    BRANCH IF     `the cover`'s `it pays money on a death`
              AND (NOT (    `the cover`'s `its term in years` AT MOST 1
                        AND `the cover`'s `it pays on a death only if by accident or a specified sickness`))
           THEN `a life policy because it pays on a death (s 9(1)(a))`
           IF `is a continuous disability policy` `the cover`
           THEN `a life policy because it is a continuous disability policy (s 9(1)(e), s 9A)`
           OTHERWISE `not a life policy under this Act`

-- s 234(1): "A life company must not intentionally carry on any insurance business other than life insurance business." (2):
-- not if the company "was carrying on general insurance business immediately before the commencement of this Act". s 11(1):
-- life insurance business is issuing life policies (and sinking fund policies) and related business; s 12A: APRA may declare
-- other insurance business (not health or property insurance) of a company "to be treated ... as if it were life insurance
-- business". APRA's declaration is asked as a fact.
-- Gloss: what my fund's insurer, or my own life insurer, may sell me as a life company. Whether my FUND may give me the cover
-- is the SIS Act (ss 68AA-68AAD), not this Act.
@export May a life insurer offer me this cover (Life Insurance Act ss 9, 9A, 12A, 234)?
GIVEN `the cover` IS A `My cover` @desc What your cover pays on, how long it runs, and whether the insurer can change it
      `APRA has declared this kind of cover life insurance business for the insurer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether APRA has made a s 12A declaration for this business
      `the insurer carried on general insurance before the Act commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer is an existing life company that already did general insurance in 1995
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a life insurer offer me this cover` IF
        (NOT (`What kind of policy is my cover` `the cover` EQUALS `not a life policy under this Act`))
    OR  `APRA has declared this kind of cover life insurance business for the insurer`
    OR  `the insurer carried on general insurance before the Act commenced`

§§ `10, Dictionary -- do I own my policy; is it a superannuation policy`

-- s 10(1): "(b) a policy is issued to the person with whom the life company enters into the contract." (2): "the owner of a
-- policy is: (a) the person to whom the policy is issued; or (b) if the rights of that person under the policy have been
-- assigned under this Act or transferred by the operation of the policy, the person who has those rights."
-- Dictionary: "superannuation policy means: (a) a life policy that is maintained for the purposes of a superannuation or
-- retirement scheme and is owned by the trustee under the scheme".
-- Gloss: inside super the trustee contracts with the insurer, so the trustee, not the member, is the owner; the member is the
-- life insured. The owner's rights in Part 10 (surrender, paid-up, forfeiture notice, replacement document) are the trustee's.
DECLARE `My policy` HAS
    `it was issued to me` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the rights under it have been assigned or transferred away from me` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the rights under it have been assigned or transferred to me` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is held by the trustee of my super fund for the fund` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Am I the owner of my policy (Life Insurance Act s 10(2))?
GIVEN `the policy` IS A `My policy` @desc To whom the policy was issued and any assignment of it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I the owner of my policy` IF
        (`the policy`'s `it was issued to me` AND (NOT `the policy`'s `the rights under it have been assigned or transferred away from me`))
    OR  `the policy`'s `the rights under it have been assigned or transferred to me`

@export Is my cover a superannuation policy (Life Insurance Act, Dictionary)?
GIVEN `the cover` IS A `My cover` @desc What your cover pays on, how long it runs, and whether the insurer can change it
      `the policy` IS A `My policy` @desc Who holds the policy
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my cover a superannuation policy` IF
        (NOT (`What kind of policy is my cover` `the cover` EQUALS `not a life policy under this Act`))
    AND `the policy`'s `it is held by the trustee of my super fund for the fund`

§§ `199 -- may I take out a policy while young`

-- s 199(1): "A person who is at least 10 but has not reached 16 may, with the written consent of a parent or a person who stands
-- in the place of a parent: (a) enter into a policy (including a life policy on his or her own life or on another life); or
-- (b) take an assignment of a policy." (2): "A person who has reached 16 but has not reached 18 has the same capacity to
-- exercise rights or powers in relation to a policy of which he or she is the owner as a person who has reached 18."
-- The Act gives a person under 10 no capacity; from 16 it says nothing about entering into a policy, only about exercising the
-- owner's rights, so entry from 16 to 18 is left to the general law of minors' contracts (INFERENCE from the silence).
DECLARE `A capacity` IS ONE OF
    `I may enter into a policy with a parent's written consent (s 199(1))`
    `I need a parent's written consent and do not have it (s 199(1))`
    `the Act gives me no capacity; the general law decides`
    `I am an adult`

@export May I take out a life policy at my age (Life Insurance Act s 199(1))?
GIVEN `my age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in completed years
      `a parent consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a parent, or someone standing in a parent's place, consented in writing
GIVETH A `A capacity`
DECIDE `May I take out a life policy at my age` IS
    BRANCH IF `my age in years` AT LEAST 18 THEN `I am an adult`
           IF `my age in years` AT LEAST 16 THEN `the Act gives me no capacity; the general law decides`
           IF `my age in years` AT LEAST 10 AND `a parent consented in writing`
           THEN `I may enter into a policy with a parent's written consent (s 199(1))`
           IF `my age in years` AT LEAST 10 THEN `I need a parent's written consent and do not have it (s 199(1))`
           OTHERWISE `the Act gives me no capacity; the general law decides`

@export Can I exercise my rights as owner of my policy as an adult can (Life Insurance Act s 199(2))?
GIVEN `my age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in completed years
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I exercise my rights as owner as an adult can` IF
    `my age in years` AT LEAST 16

§§ `218-220 -- a policy I take out for my child's advancement`

-- s 218(1): "child's advancement policy means a policy issued, before a child has reached full age, by a person other than the
-- child, which contains one or both of the following: (a) provision for payment of a sum to the executors, administrators or
-- assigns of the child on the child's death after the child reaches the vesting age; or (b) provision for payment of a sum to
-- the child ... on the child reaching an age that is at least the vesting age." "full age means ... (c) in relation to a policy
-- issued after the commencement of this Act -- the age of 16 years." "vesting age ... means: (a) an age of 10 years or more
-- specified in the policy for the purpose of defining the time at which money becomes payable under the policy; or (b) the age
-- of 25 years; whichever is the earlier."
-- Only policies issued after the Act commenced are encoded (full age 16); full age 21 or 18 for older policies is not.
-- Gloss: "issued ... by a person other than the child" is read as taken out by someone other than the child (INFERENCE: the
-- life company issues; the definition must mean the person effecting it, as s 219(3)(a) "the person effecting the policy" shows).
@export At what age does my child's advancement policy vest in my child (Life Insurance Act s 218(1))?
GIVEN `the age the policy specifies for payment` IS A NUMBER @desc The age the policy names for payment, or 0 if it names none
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the vesting age of my child's policy` IS
    IF `the age the policy specifies for payment` AT LEAST 10 AND `the age the policy specifies for payment` LESS THAN 25
    THEN `the age the policy specifies for payment`
    ELSE 25

@export Is the policy I took out on my child a child's advancement policy (Life Insurance Act s 218(1))?
GIVEN `my child's age when it was issued` IS A NUMBER @desc Your child's age when the policy was issued
      `someone other than my child took it out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (or someone other than the child) effected it
      `it pays my child, or my child's estate, at or after the vesting age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it pays the child on reaching an age, or the estate on death, at or after the vesting age
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this a child's advancement policy` IF
        `my child's age when it was issued` LESS THAN 16
    AND `someone other than my child took it out`
    AND `it pays my child, or my child's estate, at or after the vesting age`

-- s 219(2): the section "does not apply to a child's advancement policy effected by a parent ... in which it is expressly
-- provided that this section does not apply". (3): until the child reaches the vesting age "(a) the policy is the absolute
-- property ... of the person effecting the policy"; (b)(ii) who "may assign, mortgage, charge, surrender, vary or otherwise deal
-- with the policy". (4): from the vesting age "the policy is taken ... to be the absolute property of the child", subject to
-- debts and earlier dealings. s 220(1), (2): if the person effecting it "dies or becomes bankrupt ... during the child's lifetime
-- ... and before the child reaches the vesting age", their representative "holds the policy in trust for the child".
DECLARE `A holder` IS ONE OF
    `mine, as the person who took it out (s 219(3))`
    `my child's (s 219(4))`
    `held in trust for my child by my executor, administrator or trustee in bankruptcy (s 220(2))`
    `the policy's own terms decide; s 219 is excluded (s 219(2))`

@export Whose is the child's advancement policy I took out (Life Insurance Act ss 219, 220)?
GIVEN `my child's age now` IS A NUMBER @desc Your child's age now
      `the vesting age` IS A NUMBER @desc The vesting age worked out under s 218
      `the policy expressly excludes section 219` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, as a parent, you had the policy say s 219 does not apply
      `I have died or become bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have died or become bankrupt
GIVETH A `A holder`
DECIDE `Whose is my child's advancement policy` IS
    BRANCH IF `the policy expressly excludes section 219` THEN `the policy's own terms decide; s 219 is excluded (s 219(2))`
           IF `my child's age now` AT LEAST `the vesting age` THEN `my child's (s 219(4))`
           IF `I have died or become bankrupt`
           THEN `held in trust for my child by my executor, administrator or trustee in bankruptcy (s 220(2))`
           OTHERWISE `mine, as the person who took it out (s 219(3))`

§§ `200 -- an assignment of my policy`

-- s 200(1): "The rights of a person as owner of a policy may only be assigned at law under this section." (2): not effective at
-- law unless "(a) ... by memorandum of transfer" in the ASIC-approved form; "(b) the memorandum must be endorsed ... on the policy
-- document or on an annexure"; "(c) ... signed by the transferor and the transferee; (d) the assignment must be registered in a
-- register of assignments kept by the life company; (e) the date of registration must be inserted in the memorandum; (f) the
-- memorandum must be signed by the principal executive officer of the life company or" an authorised person. (8)(a): an
-- assignment otherwise made may still take effect in equity.
DECLARE `An assignment` HAS
    `it is by memorandum of transfer in the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the memorandum is endorsed on the policy document or an annexure` IS A BOOLEAN
    `both of us signed the memorandum` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the insurer registered it in its register of assignments` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the registration date is in the memorandum` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the insurer's principal executive officer, or a person authorised, signed it` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Is the assignment of my policy effective at law (Life Insurance Act s 200(2))?
GIVEN `the assignment` IS AN `An assignment` @desc How the assignment was made and registered
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the assignment of my policy effective at law` IF
        `the assignment`'s `it is by memorandum of transfer in the approved form`
    AND `the assignment`'s `the memorandum is endorsed on the policy document or an annexure`
    AND `the assignment`'s `both of us signed the memorandum`
    AND `the assignment`'s `the insurer registered it in its register of assignments`
    AND `the assignment`'s `the registration date is in the memorandum`
    AND `the assignment`'s `the insurer's principal executive officer, or a person authorised, signed it`

§§ `204, 205 -- can my creditors reach my policy, or my death money`

DECLARE `An answer under the Bankruptcy Act proviso` IS ONE OF
    `yes`
    `no`
    `the Bankruptcy Act 1966 decides`

-- s 204(1): "The rights and interests of a person under: (a) a life policy effected on his or her life; or (b) a life policy
-- effected on the life of the person's spouse or de facto partner; are not liable to be applied or made available by any
-- judgment, order or process of a court in discharge of a debt owed by the person." (2)(b): for (a), "whether or not the policy
-- is owned by the person". (3): "This section has effect subject to the Bankruptcy Act 1966."
@export Can a court make my rights under this life policy pay my debts (Life Insurance Act s 204)?
GIVEN `it is a life policy on my own life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the policy insures your life (owned by you or not)
      `it is a life policy on my spouse's or de facto partner's life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it insures your spouse's or de facto partner's life
      `I am bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are bankrupt
GIVETH AN `An answer under the Bankruptcy Act proviso`
DECIDE `Can a court make my policy pay my debts` IS
    BRANCH IF `I am bankrupt` THEN `the Bankruptcy Act 1966 decides`
           IF `it is a life policy on my own life` OR `it is a life policy on my spouse's or de facto partner's life` THEN `no`
           OTHERWISE `yes`

-- s 205(1): money payable to a person's estate on death under "a policy effected on the person's life ... is not liable to be
-- applied or made available ... in payment of the person's debts" except "(b) ... if: (i) the person had entered into a contract
-- that provided expressly for the money to be so applied; or (ii) the person had charged the money with the payment of the
-- debt; or (iii) the person gave an express direction, in his or her will ... that the money be so applied". "(c) none of the
-- following constitutes an express direction ...: (i) a mere direction that debts be paid; (ii) a charge of debts on the whole
-- or a part of the person's estate; (iii) the creation of a trust for the payment of debts." (3): subject to the Bankruptcy Act.
DECLARE `My will` IS ONE OF
    `it expressly directs that this policy money pay this debt`
    `it merely directs that my debts be paid`
    `it charges my debts on my estate`
    `it creates a trust to pay my debts`
    `it says nothing about debts`

@export When I die, can the policy money paid to my estate go to pay my debts (Life Insurance Act s 205)?
GIVEN `I contracted that the money pay this debt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made a contract expressly providing for the money to pay the debt
      `I charged the money with this debt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you charged the policy money with the debt
      `my will` IS A `My will` @desc What your will says about debts
      `I was bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your estate is in bankruptcy
GIVETH AN `An answer under the Bankruptcy Act proviso`
DECIDE `Can my death money pay my debts` IS
    BRANCH IF `I was bankrupt` THEN `the Bankruptcy Act 1966 decides`
           IF    `I contracted that the money pay this debt`
              OR `I charged the money with this debt`
              OR `my will` EQUALS `it expressly directs that this policy money pay this debt`
           THEN `yes`
           OTHERWISE `no`

§§ `207-210 -- surrender, paid-up and forfeiture: my rights as owner`

-- s 207(1): "The owner of: (a) a policy in respect of which there is no contractual obligation on the owner to make any payments
-- of premiums after the first year ...; or (b) a policy ... that has been in force for at least 3 years; may request the company
-- ... to surrender the policy." (2): "in writing". (3): "Subject to section 208 ... the company must pay to the policy owner an
-- amount equal to the surrender value of the policy less the amount of any debt owed to the company under, or secured by, the
-- policy." s 208(2): APRA "may, in writing, suspend or vary the company's obligation" (asked as a fact).
@export Must my insurer pay me the surrender value if I ask (Life Insurance Act ss 207, 208)?
GIVEN `I owe no premiums after the first year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the policy requires no premiums after its first year
      `years the policy has been in force` IS A NUMBER @desc Complete years since the policy started
      `I asked in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you asked the insurer in writing to surrender it
      `APRA has suspended or varied the insurer's obligation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether APRA has suspended or varied surrender payments under s 208
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my insurer pay me the surrender value` IF
        (`I owe no premiums after the first year` OR `years the policy has been in force` AT LEAST 3)
    AND `I asked in writing`
    AND (NOT `APRA has suspended or varied the insurer's obligation`)

-- s 207(4): if the surrender value "would be less than an amount calculated ... in accordance with the prudential standards, the
-- last-mentioned amount is the surrender value". (6): for a policy in force at commencement, not less than "the adjusted pre-1
-- July 1995 surrender value" (0 if none). Payment is the surrender value less debt; a debt larger than the value leaves nothing
-- to pay (INFERENCE: the Act does not make the owner pay the difference).
@export How much must my insurer pay me on surrender (Life Insurance Act s 207(3), (4), (6))?
GIVEN `the surrender value under the policy` IS A NUMBER @desc The surrender value the policy's terms give
      `the prudential standards minimum` IS A NUMBER @desc The minimum surrender value under the prudential standards (input; not deposited)
      `the adjusted pre-1 July 1995 surrender value` IS A NUMBER @desc For a policy in force on 1 July 1995, its adjusted surrender value then; otherwise 0
      `what I owe the insurer under or secured by the policy` IS A NUMBER @desc Policy loans and other debts secured by the policy
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much must my insurer pay me on surrender` IS
    IF `the value` GREATER THAN `what I owe the insurer under or secured by the policy`
    THEN `the value` MINUS `what I owe the insurer under or secured by the policy`
    ELSE 0
    WHERE
        `the value` MEANS
            IF `floor` GREATER THAN `the surrender value under the policy` THEN `floor` ELSE `the surrender value under the policy`
        `floor` MEANS
            IF `the adjusted pre-1 July 1995 surrender value` GREATER THAN `the prudential standards minimum`
            THEN `the adjusted pre-1 July 1995 surrender value`
            ELSE `the prudential standards minimum`

-- s 209(1): "If premiums under a policy have been paid in respect of a period of at least 3 years, the owner ... may request
-- ... (a) to vary the policy so that no further premiums are payable; and (b) to treat the policy as a paid-up policy." (2): "in
-- writing". (3): "On receiving the request, the life company must vary the policy" to a reduced amount.
@export Must my insurer make my policy paid-up if I ask (Life Insurance Act s 209)?
GIVEN `years of premiums paid` IS A NUMBER @desc The period, in years, for which premiums have been paid
      `I asked in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you asked in writing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my insurer make my policy paid-up` IF
    `years of premiums paid` AT LEAST 3 AND `I asked in writing`

-- s 210(1): "A life company must not forfeit a policy only because of the non-payment of a premium ... if: (a) at least 3 years'
-- premiums have been paid on the policy; and (b) the surrender value of the policy exceeds the total of: (i) the amount of the
-- overdue premium; and (ii) the total of any other amounts owed to the company". (2): surrender value "as at the day
-- immediately before the day on which the overdue premium falls due". (5): no forfeiture for non-payment unless "(a) the
-- company has given the policy owner a written notice" of the premium and the day it is due, stating forfeiture at the end of
-- 28 days, "and (b) at least 28 days have elapsed since: (i) the day on which the notice was given; or (ii) the day on which the
-- premium became due; whichever is the later."
DECLARE `An unpaid premium` HAS
    `years of premiums paid` IS A NUMBER
    `the surrender value the day before it fell due` IS A NUMBER
    `the overdue premium` IS A NUMBER
    `other amounts I owe the insurer under or secured by the policy` IS A NUMBER
    `the insurer gave me the written notice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE
    `the day the premium fell due` IS A DATE

@export Is my policy protected from forfeiture for this unpaid premium (Life Insurance Act s 210(1), (2))?
GIVEN `the premium` IS AN `An unpaid premium` @desc The unpaid premium, what you owe and the policy's surrender value
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my policy protected from forfeiture` IF
        `the premium`'s `years of premiums paid` AT LEAST 3
    AND `the premium`'s `the surrender value the day before it fell due` GREATER THAN
            (`the premium`'s `the overdue premium` PLUS `the premium`'s `other amounts I owe the insurer under or secured by the policy`)

@export What is the first day my insurer could forfeit my policy for this unpaid premium (Life Insurance Act s 210(5))?
GIVEN `the premium` IS AN `An unpaid premium` @desc The unpaid premium and the notice
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `What is the first day my policy could be forfeited` IS
    DATE_FROM_SERIAL ((DATE_SERIAL (`the later of` (`the premium`'s `the day the notice was given`) (`the premium`'s `the day the premium fell due`))) PLUS 28)

@export May my insurer forfeit my policy today for this unpaid premium (Life Insurance Act s 210(1), (5))?
GIVEN `the premium` IS AN `An unpaid premium` @desc The unpaid premium and the notice
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my insurer forfeit my policy today` IF
        (NOT `Is my policy protected from forfeiture` `the premium`)
    AND `the premium`'s `the insurer gave me the written notice`
    AND DATE_SERIAL `today` AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL (`What is the first day my policy could be forfeited` `the premium`)

§§ `211-213 -- payment when someone dies, without probate`

-- ss 211(1), 212(1): if the money payable by a life company to the personal representative of a deceased person under one
-- policy, or under 2 or more policies in total, "does not exceed $100,000 or such other amount as is prescribed", "the company
-- may pay the money to: (c) the spouse, de facto partner, parent, child, brother, sister, niece or nephew of the deceased
-- person; or (d) a person who satisfies the company that he or she is entitled to the property of the deceased person: (i)
-- under the deceased person's will; or (ii) under the law relating to the disposition of the property of deceased persons; or
-- (e) a person who satisfies the company that he or she is entitled to obtain probate ... or ... letters of administration".
-- (2): "without requiring the production of any probate or letters of administration". (5): money is "the total of the money
-- payable under the policy, less any debt due to the company". (4): the person paid "must apply the money in due course of
-- administration". The company's being satisfied is asked as a fact. The company MAY pay; nobody can make it.
-- Gloss: a family member of the person who died may be paid a modest policy without waiting for probate.
DECLARE `A relationship to the person who died` IS ONE OF
    `spouse`
    `de facto partner`
    `parent`
    `child`
    `brother or sister`
    `niece or nephew`
    `another relative or a friend`

@export May the insurer pay me the policy money of the person who died without probate (Life Insurance Act ss 211, 212)?
GIVEN `the money payable under all their policies with that insurer` IS A NUMBER @desc The total payable to the estate by that one insurer
      `what they owed the insurer under or secured by the policies` IS A NUMBER @desc Debts due to the insurer under or secured by the policies
      `the prescribed amount, or 0 if none is prescribed` IS A NUMBER @desc Any amount the regulations prescribe instead of $100,000 (input; not deposited)
      `my relationship` IS A `A relationship to the person who died` @desc How you were related to the person who died
      `the insurer is satisfied I take their property under the will or intestacy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer is satisfied you are entitled under the will or the intestacy rules
      `the insurer is satisfied I am entitled to probate or administration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer is satisfied you could get probate or letters of administration
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the insurer pay me without probate` IF
        (`the money payable under all their policies with that insurer` MINUS `what they owed the insurer under or secured by the policies`)
            AT MOST `the threshold`
    AND (    (NOT (`my relationship` EQUALS `another relative or a friend`))
         OR  `the insurer is satisfied I take their property under the will or intestacy`
         OR  `the insurer is satisfied I am entitled to probate or administration`)
    WHERE
        `the threshold` MEANS
            IF `the prescribed amount, or 0 if none is prescribed` GREATER THAN 0
            THEN `the prescribed amount, or 0 if none is prescribed`
            ELSE 100000

-- s 213(1): applies "if the owner of a life policy dies before the person whose life is insured by the policy" and the adjusted
-- surrender value of the policy, or of all the deceased owner's policies with that company, "is less than the prescribed
-- amount". (2): if the applicant satisfies the company that he or she is entitled "under the will or on the intestacy of the
-- deceased owner, to the benefit of the policy" or "to obtain probate ... or ... letters of administration", "the company may
-- endorse on the policy a declaration that the applicant ... is the owner". (4): the applicant "becomes ... the owner". (6):
-- adjusted surrender value is the surrender value on the day the owner died, less debt. (7): "prescribed amount means $50,000 or
-- such other amount as is prescribed".
@export Can I be made owner of a policy whose owner died before the life insured, without probate (Life Insurance Act s 213)?
GIVEN `the owner died before the person whose life is insured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the owner died while the life insured is still alive
      `the surrender values of the owner's policies with that insurer when the owner died, less debts` IS A NUMBER @desc The adjusted surrender value, in total
      `the prescribed amount, or 0 if none is prescribed` IS A NUMBER @desc Any amount the regulations prescribe instead of $50,000 (input; not deposited)
      `the insurer is satisfied I am entitled to the policy or to probate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer is satisfied you take the policy under the will or intestacy, or could get probate or administration
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be made owner without probate` IF
        `the owner died before the person whose life is insured`
    AND `the surrender values of the owner's policies with that insurer when the owner died, less debts` LESS THAN `the threshold`
    AND `the insurer is satisfied I am entitled to the policy or to probate`
    WHERE
        `the threshold` MEANS
            IF `the prescribed amount, or 0 if none is prescribed` GREATER THAN 0
            THEN `the prescribed amount, or 0 if none is prescribed`
            ELSE 50000

-- s 217(1): "if a claim arising under a policy is paid, no deductions are to be made on account of premiums or debts due to the
-- company under any other policy, except with the written consent of the claimant."
@export May my insurer deduct what I owe on my other policies from my claim (Life Insurance Act s 217)?
GIVEN `I consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, the claimant, consented in writing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my insurer deduct my other policies' debts from my claim` IF
    `I consented in writing`

§§ `221 -- my lost policy document`

-- s 221(2): the owner "may ask the company ... to issue ... a replacement policy document"; (7): "in writing". (5): "If the
-- company does not issue a replacement policy document within 6 months after it receives a request from a policy owner, the
-- policy owner may apply to a court of summary jurisdiction" for an order. The 6 months end on the same date 6 months on; the
-- owner may apply from the next day (INFERENCE on "within 6 months after").
@export May I go to a court to get a replacement for my lost policy document (Life Insurance Act s 221(5))?
GIVEN `I asked the insurer in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made a written request for a replacement
      `the day the insurer received my request` IS A DATE @desc The day the insurer received it
      `the insurer has issued a replacement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a replacement has been issued
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply to a court for a replacement policy document` IF
        `I asked the insurer in writing`
    AND (NOT `the insurer has issued a replacement`)
    AND DATE_SERIAL `today` GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL (`add months` `the day the insurer received my request` 6)

§§ `228, 229 -- suicide and war service`

-- s 228: "A life company may only avoid a life policy on the ground that the person whose life is insured by the policy
-- committed suicide if the policy expressly excludes liability in case of suicide."
@export May the insurer refuse to pay because the person insured died by suicide (Life Insurance Act s 228)?
GIVEN `the policy expressly excludes liability for suicide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the policy has an express suicide exclusion
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the insurer avoid the policy for suicide` IF
    `the policy expressly excludes liability for suicide`

-- s 229(1): a term "is void if it limits, to an amount less than the total of the sum insured and bonuses, the amount payable
-- under the policy if the life insured by the policy dies on war service." (2): not "if there is written on the policy document
-- an acknowledgment signed by the person to whom the policy was issued that the policy is subject to the term".
@export Is the war-service limit in my life policy void (Life Insurance Act s 229)?
GIVEN `the term pays less than the sum insured and bonuses on death on war service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the term cuts the payout on death on war service
      `I signed an acknowledgment of the term written on the policy document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person to whom the policy was issued signed an acknowledgment on the document
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the war-service limit void` IF
        `the term pays less than the sum insured and bonuses on death on war service`
    AND (NOT `I signed an acknowledgment of the term written on the policy document`)
